# STATUS: grammar draft. Does not run yet.
#
# tools/FrameFlow.TestBench does not exist. This file was written to test the
# script grammar in docs/adr/command-driven-testbench-host.md against a real
# reproduction, and three of that grammar's rules changed because of it. The
# invocation below is what it will be, not what works today.
#
# Signage shape: GPU zero-copy presenter, no audio sink.
#
# Converted from the Repro-Signage-NoAudio-GPU profile in
# examples/FrameFlow.Examples.AvaloniaPlayer/Properties/launchSettings.json.
#
#   dotnet run --project tools/FrameFlow.TestBench -- \
#       --presenter gpu --no-audio \
#       --script scripts/repro/signage-gpu-noaudio.bench
#
# With no audio sink the player paces video off WallClockSource rather than the
# audio sample counter (ADR-0003), while the composition-interop presenter keeps
# D3D11VA frames on the GPU through present (ADR-0061). That pair is the signage
# deployment's shape, and it is the pair this script pins.

require presenter gpu
require audio off

load tests/corpus/files/test-1080p-h264-aac.mp4

# 1920x1080, 30 fps, 3.0s — scripts/generate-test-corpus.cs
expect duration == 3.0s +- 100ms

play
wait state == Playing
wait sink.presented >= 15            # half a second of frames; let it settle

# No audio sink, so there is nothing to drift against. Asserted rather than
# assumed: a null drift read as zero would make an A/V assertion pass on a
# pipeline that never produced timed audio at all.
expect drift == null
expect out.active == false

# FramesCommitted stays zero on the WriteableBitmap path, so this catches a
# silent fall back to the CPU surface — the failure where the repro runs green
# because it stopped reproducing anything.
expect sink.committed >= 1

# Hardware decode without naming a backend, so the same line holds on Linux
# under VAAPI.
expect video.backend != null

mark warm
wait state == Ended timeout 8s

expect since warm video.errors == 0
expect since warm video.shed == 0
expect since warm sync.dropped == 0
expect since warm sink.dropped == 0
expect since warm sink.presented >= 25/s

diag
